It is problematic with boolean expressions that we are not considered in the previous IF, eg. functions that return a boolean

```
from employees | where to_boolean(to_string(emp_no))
```

```
{
    "error": {
        "root_cause": [
            {
                "type": "esql_illegal_argument_exception",
                "reason": "Expected a FieldAttribute or MetadataAttribute but received [to_boolean(to_string(emp_no))]"
            }
        ],
        "type": "esql_illegal_argument_exception",
        "reason": "Expected a FieldAttribute or MetadataAttribute but received [to_boolean(to_string(emp_no))]"
    },
    "status": 500
}
```

